    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_boundaries_repair_diplomatic_language",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-boundaries-repair-01",
        "slug": "c1-boundaries-repair-diplomatic-language",
        "title": "Diplomatic challenge and disagreement",
        "rule_summary": "Challenge an idea rather than a person, acknowledge intent, and soften direct negatives while keeping the substantive point clear.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "به‌جای شخص، ایده را به چالش می‌کشیم؛ نیت را می‌پذیریم و بدون مبهم کردن اصل پیام، منفی مستقیم را نرم‌تر می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "I see the logic, though I'm not convinced the assumption holds in this case.",
            "fa": "منطقش را می‌بینم، هرچند قانع نشده‌ام این فرض در این مورد برقرار باشد."
          },
          {
            "en": "That may be true in principle, but the practical constraints are different.",
            "fa": "در اصل شاید درست باشد، اما محدودیت‌های عملی متفاوت‌اند."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_boundaries_repair_cleft_sentences",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-boundaries-repair-02",
        "slug": "c1-boundaries-repair-cleft-sentences",
        "title": "Cleft sentences for focus",
        "rule_summary": "Use what-clauses and it-clefts to place deliberate emphasis on the most important part of a message.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "با what-clause و it-cleft بخش مهم پیام را برجسته می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "What concerns me most is the lack of independent oversight.",
            "fa": "چیزی که بیشتر نگرانم می‌کند نبود نظارت مستقل است."
          },
          {
            "en": "It was the timing, rather than the decision itself, that caused the problem.",
            "fa": "زمان‌بندی بود، نه خود تصمیم، که مشکل را ایجاد کرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c1_boundaries_repair_concession_rebuttal",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-boundaries-repair-03",
        "slug": "c1-boundaries-repair-concession-rebuttal",
        "title": "Concession followed by rebuttal",
        "rule_summary": "Acknowledge a reasonable opposing point before limiting it or presenting a stronger counterargument.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "ابتدا یک نکته منطقی از طرف مقابل را می‌پذیریم و سپس دامنه آن را محدود می‌کنیم یا پاسخ قوی‌تری می‌دهیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Granted, the process is faster; that does not necessarily make it fairer.",
            "fa": "درست است که روند سریع‌تر است؛ اما لزوماً عادلانه‌تر نیست."
          },
          {
            "en": "While that concern is valid, it overlooks the cost of doing nothing.",
            "fa": "با اینکه آن نگرانی معتبر است، هزینه هیچ کاری نکردن را نادیده می‌گیرد."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C1",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c1_boundaries_repair_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c1-boundaries-repair-01",
        "title": "Boundaries & Relationship Repair: part 1",
        "setting": "podcast planning call",
        "cefr": "C1",
        "topic": "polite-language",
        "characters": [
          "Ella",
          "Amir"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Ella",
            "text": "Where do you think the strongest part of the case is?",
            "translation_fa": "فکر می‌کنی قوی‌ترین بخش استدلال کجاست؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "Amir",
            "text": "A boundary is clearer when it describes what you will do, not only what you want the other person to stop doing.",
            "translation_fa": "مرز وقتی روشن‌تره که بگه خودت چه کاری می‌کنی، نه فقط اینکه طرف مقابل چه کاری رو متوقف کنه."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Ella",
            "text": "And where would you qualify it?",
            "translation_fa": "و کجاش رو با احتیاط یا قید بیشتری بیان می‌کردی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "Amir",
            "text": "The breach of trust was not just the mistake itself; it was the decision to hide it after being asked directly.",
            "translation_fa": "نقض اعتماد فقط خود اشتباه نبود؛ تصمیم به پنهان کردنش بعد از سؤال مستقیم بود."
          }
        ],
        "status": "approved"
      }
